  "verbalization": "Namogenin C is shown to have a target relationship with the CD70 antigen through multiple pathways, all of which lead to the Vacuolar ATP synthase subunit S1. This subunit is identified as a target of several structurally diverse compounds, including [(2S,4R,4aS,4bR,7R,8aR,9R,10aS)-4-benzoyloxy-7-ethenyl-8a,9-dihydroxy-1,1,4a,7-tetramethyl-3,5,8-trioxo-4,4b,6,9,10,10a-hexahydro-2H-phenanthren-2-yl] benzoate and (2R,3R,4R,5R,6S)-2-[[7-hydroxy-2-(4-hydroxy-3-methoxyphenyl)-5-(3-hydroxypropyl)-2,3-dihydro-1-benzofuran-3-yl]methoxy]-6-methyloxane-3,4,5-triol. These compounds are all linked to the CD70 antigen through a common intermediate, the Vacuolar ATP synthase subunit S1. The consistent presence of this relationship across different molecular structures suggests a potential mechanism involving the targeting of this subunit, which in turn may influence the CD70 antigen. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Namogenin C and CD70 antigen through the modulation of the Vacuolar ATP synthase subunit S1, though the exact biological role of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
